{
  "requirement": "Each assessment MUST have a separate JSON usage record under\n`<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json` using\n{cite}`requirements.configuration.state_location`.\nIt MUST identify its format version, run, project root, subject kind and full\nname, start time, backend and model when known, end time when finished, outcome,\naccepted determination kind (`true`, `false`, or `FIXME`) when present, and\nwhether evidence was written. It MUST record the selected output destination in\n`evidence_output` as `file` or `stdout`; a successful write to either destination\nMUST set `evidence_written` to true. Usage recording MUST remain outside the\nproject in stdout mode. FIXME entry text MUST NOT be stored in usage records.\nFailed, cancelled, or unfinished\nruns MUST remain distinguishable from completed judgments. Records MUST persist\nfor later review without storing source text, prompts, responses, or rationale.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.authoring.usage_storage`. I did not request implementation source. The mapping below is by obligation.\n\n- **Separate record per assessment at `<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json`.**\n  - `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported]` checks that the single file under `habeas/authoring/usage` is named `<run_id>.json`. A second `--force` run adds a second file and leaves the first byte-identical.\n  - `fn[citation_reviews_are_confirmed_with_fresh_targeted_conversations]` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` checks that two assessments give two logs with different `run_id`s.\n  - `fn[confirm_runs_a_second_assessment_with_its_own_usage_record]` checks separate subject labels for the first and second assessment.\n- **Identifying fields.**\n  - The same CLI test asserts `version` 1, `run_id`, canonical `project_root`, `subject`, `subject_kind`, `backend`, `model`, and `start_time_ms <= end_time_ms`.\n  - `fn[usage_subject_kind_is_known_before_sources_are_prepared]` checks the kind noun for requirement, example, citation review and site review.\n  - `fn[usage_record_of_an_early_failure_identifies_its_subject_kind]` checks that an early failure still records the kind.\n  - `fn[adaptive_routes_fresh_assessments_and_records_each_model]` checks that the model is recorded per run.\n  - `fn[authoring_uses_nearest_workspace_configuration_without_a_user_file]` checks the model value.\n- **Determination kind.**\n  - The `true` kind is asserted in `fn[stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files]`.\n  - The `false` kind is asserted in that test and in `fn[false_is_a_completed_assessment]`.\n  - The `FIXME` kind is asserted in `fn[ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free]` and in the stdout test.\n  - The determination is null when submissions are missing, duplicated or invalid (`fn[missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence]`).\n- **`evidence_output` and `evidence_written`.**\n  - The stdout test asserts `evidence_output` is `stdout` and `evidence_written` is true, across true, false and FIXME determinations and in verbose mode.\n  - The file mode is asserted as `file` in the CLI record test.\n  - The batch tests assert `evidence_written` true on completed file-mode runs.\n  - Failure cases assert `evidence_written` false for both destinations. These are the invalid-submission test, `fn[failed_evidence_write_keeps_the_accepted_judgment_in_usage]`, and the aborted-assessment check in `fn[a_denied_mandatory_input_aborts_only_its_assessment]`.\n  - `fn[live_bedrock_authoring]` asserts the same stdout values for a live run.\n- **Usage stays outside the project in stdout mode.** `fn[usage_state_inside_the_project_is_refused_before_creating_it]` runs both file mode and `--stdout` with the state root inside the project. It asserts a refusal with the \"must be outside the project repository\" message, empty stdout, and that the directory is never created. The stdout test confirms the usage file exists at the reported location.\n- **No FIXME entry text.** The FIXME CLI test asserts that the serialized usage lacks `#125`, which is the FIXME entry, while `determination` is `\"FIXME\"`.\n- **Failed, cancelled and unfinished runs are distinguishable.**\n  - `fn[cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals]` asserts the initial record is `unfinished` with a null end time, and the cancelled record has `outcome` `cancelled` and an end time.\n  - `fn[failed_persistence_records_failure_or_cancellation_and_retains_the_cause]` covers failed versus cancelled persistence failures, including when the usage file itself is obstructed. It asserts the `failed`/`cancelled` outcome, `evidence_written` false, an end time, and a null determination.\n  - `completed` appears in the batch, CLI and `fn[input_metadata_counts_components_and_reads_without_persisting_source]` tests.\n- **No source text, prompts, responses or rationale.**\n  - `fn[input_metadata_counts_components_and_reads_without_persisting_source]` asserts that sentinel source, requirement, definition, builtin and file names are absent from the serialized file.\n  - `fn[tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text]` asserts that model-supplied tool names are absent.\n  - The FIXME CLI test asserts that `SECRET_REQUIREMENT_TEXT`, `SECRET_DEFINITION_TEXT`, `SECRET_SOURCE_PAYLOAD`, `SECRET_RATIONALE` and the credential are absent.\n  - `fn[authoring_uses_nearest_workspace_configuration_without_a_user_file]` asserts that the workspace API key is absent.\n- **Cited `requirements.configuration.state_location`.** The tests apply the state root through `XDG_STATE_HOME` in the fixture. An unusable state location (a file blocker, or unset XDG and HOME) fails with nonempty stderr and empty stdout before any model request. The evidence is preserved and no success is claimed. The Windows `LOCALAPPDATA` branch belongs to the cited requirement, so it is not reassessed here.\n\nI found no plausible requirement-violating behavior that these assertions would accept. The `{test}` markings are present on all of the tests above.",
  "references": "4b1a5eae2f231154488e098b77c5bd668b7877063fefff2bca6d98d2d5789850",
